-- ===========================================================================
-- Warlock: tooltip corrections
-- ===========================================================================
--
-- Three client-side display bugs from woa_2026_08_01_04/06/07.sql.
-- Server-side behaviour is UNCHANGED by this file -- every CalcValue() the
-- C++ reads stays exactly what it was.
--
-- BUG 1: "3 to 2% more damage" / "2 to 1%"  (EffectDieSides = 0)
--   The client renders a value as the range  [BasePoints + 1 .. BasePoints +
--   DieSides].  With DieSides = 1 both ends collapse to BasePoints + 1 and a
--   single number is shown.  With DieSides = 0 the max end becomes
--   BasePoints + 0, i.e. one LESS than the min -- so the client prints a
--   backwards range like "3 to 2".
--
--   The server agrees with the client only at DieSides = 1:
--   SpellEffectInfo::CalcValue (SpellInfo.cpp:431) does
--     DieSides == 0 -> BasePoints          (no adjustment)
--     DieSides == 1 -> BasePoints + 1
--   so restoring DieSides = 1 and dropping BasePoints by one keeps every
--   computed value identical while fixing the tooltip.  This is also the
--   convention CLAUDE.md documents ("to display N, set BasePoints to N-1")
--   and what Blizzard itself ships (e.g. 54370 Nether Protection:
--   BasePoints -31 / DieSides 1 -> -30).
--
--   Values are therefore unchanged in effect:
--     Infernal Bargain   dmg/shard 2/3/4, crit/shard 1/1/2, reduction 15/20/25
--     Sacrifice the Weak 1% damage reduction and 1% crit per Soul Shard
--     Wailing Soul       5% damage taken reduction per stack
--
-- BUG 2: Wailing Souls said "101% chance"
--   The description uses $h, which reads the spell's DBC ProcChance -- but
--   the real chance lived only in `spell_proc`, which the client cannot see.
--   ProcChance had been parked at 101 so that spell_proc was the sole gate.
--   Fixed by making the DBC the single source of truth: each rank's
--   ProcChance carries its real value (34/67/100) and the spell_proc rows
--   set Chance = 0, which makes SpellMgr fall back to the per-rank DBC value
--   (SpellMgr.cpp:2083, evaluated inside the rank loop).  Tooltip and
--   behaviour can no longer drift apart.
--
--   NOTE: Burning Soul and Molten Rain are NOT affected -- their
--   descriptions use $s1 (effect basepoints), which already display
--   correctly, and their DieSides were left at 1.
-- ===========================================================================


